\description{
A small, bundled collection of simulated quarterly series, each paired with
its \strong{true nonseasonal counterfactual} -- the series one would observe if
the seasonality were absent. Because the counterfactual is known by
construction, \code{ssi_examples} lets vignettes, examples, and tests measure a
seasonal adjustment's accuracy \emph{against truth}, a demonstration no real
dataset permits.

There is exactly one series per identification "world". The world is the
modelling commitment that the phase rule encodes (filter-versus-components
identification is not testable at second order; see \code{\link[=seas_ssi]{seas_ssi()}} and
\code{vignette("two-worlds")}), so each world exercises a different correct
adjustment:
\describe{
\item{\code{"filter"}}{Shared-innovation (deconvolution) world: the seasonal
series and its counterfactual are driven by the \emph{same} innovations. The
minimum-phase rule (\code{phase_rule = "minimum"}) is correct here.}
\item{\code{"components"}}{Independent-seasonal world: an added seasonal
component with its own innovations sits on top of the nonseasonal part.
The zero-phase / Wiener-shrinkage rule (\code{phase_rule = "zero"}) is correct
here.}
\item{\code{"line"}}{Deterministic seasonality: a fixed, frozen quarterly
pattern (a line spectrum) rather than a stochastic band.}
}
}
\details{
All three series are quarterly (\code{s = 4}), length \code{n = 120} (30 years,
\verb{2000 Q1 .. 2029 Q4}), generated after a spin-up of \code{400} discarded quarters
from zero initial conditions, from a single master seed (\code{20260722}) consumed
in world order (filter, then components, then line). The session's
calibration is used throughout: nonseasonal AR(1) coefficient \code{phi = 0.5},
seasonal coefficient \code{Phi = 0.9}, and (deterministic-line only) amplitudes
\code{A12 = 1.5} and \code{A3 = 2.0}. Every innovation stream is standard normal
(\code{sd = 1}). Writing \code{B} for the backshift operator (\verb{B x_t = x_\{t-1\}}):

\strong{filter world.} The observed series and its counterfactual \code{xNS}
share one innovation stream \code{eps}:
\deqn{(1 - \phi B)(1 - \Phi B^{s})\, x_t = \varepsilon_t, \qquad
      (1 - \phi B)\, x^{NS}_t = \varepsilon_t.}
Equivalently \verb{x_t = phi x_\{t-1\} + Phi x_\{t-4\} - phi Phi x_\{t-5\} + eps_t} and
\verb{xNS_t = phi xNS_\{t-1\} + eps_t}. Applying \verb{(1 - phi B)} to both definitions
cancels the nonseasonal factor and yields the exact deconvolution identity
\deqn{x^{NS}_t = x_t - \Phi\, x_{t-4},}
which holds on the retained window to machine precision and is the generation
cross-check. \code{truth} is \code{xNS}.

\strong{components world.} A nonseasonal AR(1) part \code{a} (the truth) and an
independent seasonal AR part \code{s}, with their own innovation streams \code{u} and
\code{eta}, are added:
\deqn{(1 - \phi B)\, a_t = u_t, \qquad (1 - \Phi B^{s})\, s_t = \eta_t,
      \qquad x_t = a_t + s_t.}
\code{truth} is \code{a}; by construction \code{x_t - truth_t = s_t} exactly, and
\verb{(1 - Phi B^s)} applied to \code{x - truth} recovers \code{eta}.

\strong{line world.} A nonseasonal AR(1) part \code{a} (the truth) plus a fixed,
deterministic quarterly pattern:
\deqn{(1 - \phi B)\, a_t = u_t, \qquad
      p_t = A_{12}\cos(\pi t/2) + A_{12}\sin(\pi t/2) + A_{3}\cos(\pi t),
      \qquad x_t = a_t + p_t.}
The pattern has power only at the annual harmonic (\code{pi/2}, amplitude \code{A12})
and the semiannual / Nyquist harmonic (\code{pi}, amplitude \code{A3}) -- a line
spectrum. \code{truth} is \code{a}; by construction \code{x_t - truth_t = p_t} exactly, and
the pattern is stored in \code{params$pattern}.
}
\examples{
# The filter-world series and its true nonseasonal counterfactual:
fw    <- ssi_examples[ssi_examples$world == "filter", ]
x     <- fw$x[[1]]
truth <- fw$truth[[1]]

# The defining deconvolution identity holds to machine precision:
Phi <- fw$params[[1]]$Phi
max(abs(truth[5:120] - (x[5:120] - Phi * x[1:116])))  # ~1e-15

# Adjust, then compare against the known truth (demeaned; the shared-
# innovation gain at frequency zero is not removable -- see the vignettes):
adj <- seas_adjust(x, phase_rule = "minimum")
dm  <- function(z) z - mean(z)
c(none = sqrt(mean((dm(x)             - dm(truth))^2)),
  adj  = sqrt(mean((dm(adjusted(adj)) - dm(truth))^2)))
}
